course: dictionary
lesson: 4696
title: Honest and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Honest is a word about truth. Being honest means telling the truth, and not lying, cheating or stealing. «If Gran says "keep the change", telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift.» Telling Gran the truth about the money is what makes the gift honest.
explain: An honest answer is true and sincere, which means you really mean it. An honest mistake is a mistake you make without meaning to trick anyone. «In Kai's game a player kept flying through walls, which no honest player can do.» Here honest means playing fairly and following the rules.
explain: Honest does not mean unkind. You can tell the truth and still be gentle. Look at the words around honest: when a sentence talks about trust, owning up or giving things back, honest probably means truthful and fair.
fact: Honest means telling the truth and not lying, cheating or stealing.
fact: An honest mistake is a mistake made without meaning to trick anyone.
fact: «To be honest» means I am telling you what I really think.
fact: Being honest builds trust: you own up to mistakes, give back things that are not yours, and do not copy in tests.
fact: «Honest shops last because buyers come back.»
exercise: «If Gran says "keep the change", telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift.» What does honest mean in this sentence? | Spending the money as fast as you can | *Telling the truth about the money | Hiding how much change is left | Losing the change
exercise: Which action is honest? | Telling a lie to get out of trouble | Taking a toy that belongs to someone else | Copying answers from a friend in a test | *Owning up when you break a vase
exercise: Priya says, "I didn't mean to spill your juice, it was an honest mistake." What does honest mistake mean? | *A mistake made without meaning to trick anyone | A mistake made on purpose to trick someone | A mistake that is always very big | A mistake that someone else made
test: Which word means telling the truth and not cheating? | Kind | Quick | *Honest | Brave
test: «In Kai's game a player kept flying through walls, which no honest player can do.» What does this suggest about an honest player? | They never play games | They can fly through walls | They always win | *They play fairly and follow the rules
exam: Does honest mean unkind? Choose the best answer. | *No, you can be honest and gentle at the same time | Yes, because honest means cruel | Yes, honest people are always rude | No, honest means quiet
